course: dictionary
lesson: 9412
title: Words that sound like their meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like the noise they describe. Squawk is one of them. Say it out loud and it sounds a little like a bird's harsh cry. «When it squawked, she stopped» tells you the timer made a loud, harsh noise, and the sound of the word helps you picture it.
explain: Squawk can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, it means to make that cry: «Priya's timer squawked.» As a noun, it is the cry itself: «The timer gave one loud squawk.» Look at the words around it to see which one you have.
explain: Squawk can also mean to complain loudly. If someone says, «The kids squawked about bedtime», they are not making bird noises. They are complaining. Ask yourself: does the sentence describe a sound, or an unhappy complaint?
fact: Squawk means to make a loud, harsh cry, like a parrot or a scared chicken.
fact: A squawk is that loud, harsh cry.
fact: In informal English, to squawk means to complain loudly.
fact: Squawk is an onomatopoeia, a word that sounds like the noise it describes.
fact: A pilot sets a squawk code, a number that helps air traffic control identify the plane.
exercise: «Priya's timer squawked, so she stopped.» What does squawked mean? | Whispered softly | Went to sleep | *Made a loud, harsh cry | Ran quickly across the kitchen
exercise: Which word means the loud cry itself in this sentence? «The parrot gave a loud squawk.» | loud | gave | *squawk | parrot
exercise: Dad says, «The kids are squawking about bedtime.» What does squawking mean here? | *Complaining loudly | Singing softly | Counting the stars | Dancing in a circle
test: «The seagulls squawked over the chip shop.» What does squawked suggest? | Soft, gentle singing | *Loud, harsh cries | Deep, low snoring | Quiet humming
test: Why does a pilot set a squawk code? | To make the plane fly faster | To warn passengers about lunch | To turn the radio off | *To help air traffic control identify the plane
exam: Squawk sounds like the noise it describes. What is that kind of word called? | Context clue | Antonym | Synonym | *Onomatopoeia
